WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.520
When it comes to beings with fearsome reputations,
there are few SCPs that are as widely dreaded

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:11.130
as the hard-to-destroy reptile SCP-682.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:15.960
No sane mortal would ever choose to face such
a creature, and its overwhelming ferocity

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:23.180
and strength have even given the reincarnating
warrior SCP-076-2 Abel pause on more than

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:24.460
one occasion.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.390
But then again, the sane aren’t exactly
in high demand at the SCP Foundation or at

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:36.579
equivalent organizations formed for the purpose
of battling anomalous and supernatural entities.

00:00:36.579 --> 00:00:41.030
Organizations such as the Public Safety Devil
Hunters from the popular Manga and Anime Chainsaw

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:46.880
Man count numerous peculiar individuals among
their ranks, and sometimes the best of the

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.590
best are marked by a distinctive tendency
for out-of-the-box thinking.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:54.790
That’s putting it politely, at least.

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:59.879
But this isn’t the story of some aberrant
loser freakazoid - no, definitely not.

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:04.689
The heroine of this tale is none other than
the mightiest and most charismatic future

00:01:04.689 --> 00:01:09.650
nobel prize winner ever to grace the rest
of us shameful worms with her presence.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:13.659
The invincible and dearly beloved blood fiend
Power!

00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:18.930
Who just so happens to be the undisputed best
character in Chainsaw Man and all of fiction

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:19.950
as well.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:25.159
It appeared to be an unusually boring day
at Public Safety, and for this, Kobeni was

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:26.159
grateful.

00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:30.400
The young woman had come to expect the absolute
worst from her job as a devil hunter - as

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.920
her assignments usually entailed facing down
hellish entities born from the very fears

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.270
of the human race.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:40.290
While one would think that someone who worked
so diligently in the field would have grown

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:46.799
numb to it all, Kobeni still very much retained
her anxieties: both on and off the job.

00:01:46.799 --> 00:01:52.090
At least all she had to do today was file
paperwork from one of Public Safety’s like-minded

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:56.520
partners in supernatural management: The SCP
Foundation.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:01.509
It was a safe and harmless task, aside from
the risk of paper cuts and the associated

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:04.650
potential for the Paper Cut Devil to show
up.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:09.009
Even so, Kobeni would do her best to make
this rare moment of peace last as long as

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:10.009
possible.

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:11.009
“Witness me, fools!

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:12.009
For I am the great Power!”

00:02:12.009 --> 00:02:13.009
A voice cried from down the hallway.

00:02:13.009 --> 00:02:14.480
Oh no, not her.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:15.480
Kobeni thought.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.670
Why is she even at work today?

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:20.610
She’s a fighter for division four, and she’s
not good at anything else.

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:25.280
Loud, exaggerated footsteps rang out through
the hallway as the blood fiend stomped through

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.730
the offices of public safety.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:32.910
Kobeni wanted to shrink until she vanished
from sight or let herself sink into the floor.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:37.349
Her desire to not have to see Power today
was so great that she contemplated opening

00:02:37.349 --> 00:02:41.280
a window and climbing down to the side of
the building to the ground floor.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.379
Please don’t come this way.

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:47.910
Kobeni was still carrying a heavy stack of
freshly filed paperwork, and she didn’t

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:51.489
want her tireless efforts at organization
to go to waste.

00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:55.540
She looked frantically at the cabinets in
the storage room she was in, hoping to find

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.920
enough space for her to crawl into and make
herself scarce.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:01.120
But it was too late!

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:05.030
Power slammed open the door of the storage
room and announced her presence.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:09.680
The shock was so great that Kobeni screamed
and flung the stack of SCP Foundation papers

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.340
all over the ground.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.560
She clutched her fast-beating heart, unable
to attend to the mess immediately.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:19.690
Kobeni hadn’t had to experience a fright
that sudden since the time that she was sent

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.590
to hunt the Jump Scare Devil.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.909
The poor girl could never have a surprise
party thrown in her honor again.

00:03:25.909 --> 00:03:31.120
True to her nature, Power immediately reprimanded
Kobeni for dropping the papers - stating that

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.970
her workmanship was sloppy and that Power
herself could easily carry ten times the amount

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.120
of paper.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.600
Kobeni tried not to let the chiding of her
co-worker affect her mood.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:45.540
She scoped down and began up the papers, but
much to her chagrin: Power decided to help

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.170
with this task as well.

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:50.830
The blood fiend began grabbing the papers
and stacking them as assertively as possible

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:56.120
on the nearest surfaces, resulting in many
crumbled edges and uneven piles.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:01.310
Kobeni attempted, albeit hesitantly, to correct
Power’s people collection method, only to

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:02.740
be met with more scorn.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:03.740
“You don’t know how to stack paper like
me!”

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:04.740
Power laughed.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:05.740
“And that’s why I’ll be a millionaire
someday, and you’ll still be here.”

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:06.740
Kobeni nearly cried.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:09.510
This was just too much for her to handle,
especially on what was supposed to be a calm

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:10.510
day.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:13.900
That was when Power picked up one the files
and began to read.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:21.060
It was a record of the infamous cross-test
between SCP-682 and SCP-076-2.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:27.040
Since Public Safety had previously assisted
the Foundation in re-containing SCP-076-2,

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:31.390
there had been an agreement to send copies
of all relevant documents involving Abel over

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:34.530
to Japan in case of another incident.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:38.940
As Power struggled through the scientific
language and specifics, she began to envision

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.650
her own version of the events that played
out on the page.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:49.070
She imagined herself as Abel, facing off in
pitched combat against SCP-682 and giving

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:51.600
the terrible lizard a run for its money in
the process.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.750
In the mere seconds it took for Power to finish
reading the document, she had not only concocted

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:02.160
an entire epic battle in mind - but was not
fully convinced that her fantasy was indistinguishable

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.550
from one of her own lived experiences.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:10.060
In her head, Power had definitely fought against
SCP-682.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:15.890
And she’d do it again in a heartbeat: just
to teach that overgrown reptile another lesson.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:19.930
Power asked Kobeni if she had ever told her
about the time that the blood fiend had totally

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:21.830
defeated SCP-682.

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:26.880
Kobeni, still clinging to her increasingly
frail understanding of reality, responded

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:28.410
with confusion.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.270
What was she talking about?

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.780
Nobody in Public Safety had fought against
an SCP other than 076-2.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:41.100
There was no possible way that Power was telling
the truth, but the scariest part was: Power

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:44.009
herself didn’t even know that she was lying.

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:49.610
The blood fiend began to relate the sordid
details of her pulse-pounding fight with SCP-682

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.320
to Kobeni in great detail.

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:56.020
Kobeni, for her part, was too emotionally
drained at this point to try and stop her.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.020
“So begins the greatest tale ever told,
mortal!”

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.020
Power began.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:00.759
It all started at the bowling alley, where
Power was hanging out with her much less intelligent

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:03.190
friends: Aki and Denji.

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:07.800
The blood fiend had just finished winning
her fifth perfectly scored game in a row when

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:11.750
some shady characters a few lanes over decided
to cause some trouble.

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:15.120
The leader of this little gang was none other
than SCP-682.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:19.620
“The way you bowl is disgusting!”

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.680
The troublemaking lizard said.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.560
This wicked remark would not be stood for!

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:28.420
Not in the proud bowling establishment that
Power had founded with her own money and had

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:32.150
achieved several years of successful business
running herself!

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:35.840
The bowling alley was a pillar of the community,
and she was the owner.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:39.150
There would be no further disrespect on her
watch.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:43.140
Power put up her dukes and got ready to bring
the pain down on SCP-682.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:49.060
Aki and Denji were too terrified to help her
out as usual, but they did their best to cheer

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:50.720
their leader on from the sidelines.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:51.720
“Stand back, weaklings!

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:52.720
The mighty Power has got this!”

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:57.920
SCP-682 also dismissed its minions and crawled
forward like the big ugly lizard that it was.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:02.060
It obviously didn’t know better, which is
why it wasn’t backing down in the face of

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:05.180
the greatest devil hunter that the world had
ever known.

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:08.620
Either way, this would be a brawl for the
ages.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:13.240
Rather than cause damage to her beloved place
of business, Power suggested that she and

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.310
her opponent took this fight outside.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:20.470
Despite its uncouth demeanor, the reptile
had a healthy appreciation for the fine sport

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:27.139
of bowling and, most especially, this particular
excellently run five-star bowling alley.

00:07:27.139 --> 00:07:31.389
It agreed to step outside in the interest
of not bringing bowling into this intensely

00:07:31.389 --> 00:07:33.190
personal grudge match.

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:37.330
But then again – wasn’t the fight about
bowling?

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:43.039
Power and SCP-682 walked outside the bowling
alley into a vast, trackless wasteland: the

00:07:43.039 --> 00:07:47.740
perfect place for both of them to go all out
without hurting any civilians.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:53.190
Using her ability to control and reshape her
own blood, Power constructed an enormous crimson

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:59.650
mallet that she was able to wield gracefully
in both her hands despite its incredible size.

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:01.500
SCP-682 readied itself.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:06.691
It had faced many different kinds of humanoid
weapon wielders before, including Abel, but

00:08:06.691 --> 00:08:10.250
it was too clever of an adversary to let its
guard down.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:14.629
Especially because, in this case, the blood
fiend it was fighting was a remarkable businesswoman

00:08:14.629 --> 00:08:18.490
and an olympic gold medalist in everything.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:21.169
The reptile certainly let its guard down.

00:08:21.169 --> 00:08:24.300
Power held the hammer above her head and jumped
high into the air.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:28.440
If she wanted to, she could have circled the
globe in a single leap, but out of respect

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:33.820
for the fact that SCP-682 was a paying customer
at her establishment - she decided to hold

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.459
back for the first attack at least.

00:08:36.459 --> 00:08:41.469
Nonetheless, she brought the hammer down on
the hard-to-destroy reptile with supreme force.

00:08:41.469 --> 00:08:47.350
SCP-682 was smashed into the ground with such
force that a crater opened up beneath its

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:48.350
body.

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:52.230
The reptile itself didn’t seem especially
damaged, but the effects on the surrounding

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:56.720
environment were certainly dramatic and fitting
for an ultimate showdown.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:01.590
SCP-682 shook off the blow and pounced on
Power with such sudden ferocity that even

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:03.750
she couldn’t remain on her feet.

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:07.649
She tumbled back through the dust and debris
of the wasteland for several miles before

00:09:07.649 --> 00:09:10.230
catching himself and standing back up.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:13.640
Remarkably, there wasn’t even a scratch
on her.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:18.680
She pointed and laughed at SCP-682, mocking
it for its weakness and stupidity.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:19.680
“You’ll have to do better than that, Lizard
Devil.” Power said.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:23.910
The reptile grinned wickedly and responded
with a mocking laugh of its own.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:27.899
The creature had intentionally taken a hit
from a Power in order to better understand

00:09:27.899 --> 00:09:29.459
her fighting moves.

00:09:29.459 --> 00:09:32.670
Who wouldn’t want to steal those masterful
techniques, after all?

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:37.980
They’re just too good to resist making a
cheap copy of, and from what Power could remember

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:43.620
from her speed read of the file: that appeared
to be SCP-682’s whole thing.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:48.480
Soon, a barding of blood-red armor appeared
around SCP-682’s body.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.540
In the short time that it had been fighting
Power, it had clearly learned how to manipulate

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:57.260
its own blood and was now even stronger for
it.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:00.420
“Hahaha, now I’m as strong as you!

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:01.420
I can’t lose!”

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:02.420
SCP-682 barked at Power.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:03.420
But she was quick to respond: “Annoying
lizard!

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:05.339
I was already as strong as me before this
fight even began!

00:10:05.339 --> 00:10:06.339
Now let’s end this!

00:10:06.339 --> 00:10:07.339
For bowling!”

00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:08.709
She swung her mallet in a show of force.

00:10:08.709 --> 00:10:12.740
The two combatants, now both wielding the
near-limitless powers of the Blood Fiend,

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:15.500
charged at each other across the battlefield.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:20.250
This was not just a mere sparring match anymore:
it was a fight for the fate of the entire

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:21.250
world.

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:24.760
Snapping back to reality, Power’s retelling
of the story had devolved into a series of

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:27.730
random exclamations and sound effects.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:32.310
Kobeni was now finding the events incredibly
hard to follow, but thankfully she had been

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:36.529
able to use Power’s highly distractible
mannerisms to finish restacking the files

00:10:36.529 --> 00:10:38.120
from the foundation.

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:43.720
Not a minute too soon either, as both she
and Power’s boss, Makima, stepped into the

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:44.720
storage room.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:48.701
Apparently, Makima was in the process of doing
a headcount of all employees who had come

00:10:48.701 --> 00:10:52.790
into work today as any normal and benevolent
superior would.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:56.800
She had been looking for Kobeni and Power
for some time now and was surprised to find

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:58.750
them here, of all places.

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:02.959
Kobeni explained that she had been putting
away the last of the SCP Foundation files

00:11:02.959 --> 00:11:06.220
and would gladly accept whatever new post
she was given.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:12.340
But Power wasn’t done with her current SCP-682
fascination and turned to Makima, hoping to

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:14.820
be encouraged to continue the story.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:18.960
Makima simply smiled and implied that if Power
was so inclined to settle her score with the

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:23.730
hard-to-destroy reptile, Public Safety could
get in contact with the Foundation and have

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:26.959
her on flight to Site 19 by that evening.

00:11:26.959 --> 00:11:30.800
Power suddenly realized that she came down
with a terrible case of whatever crippling

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:35.180
disease would be a sufficient excuse for her
not to do that to this moment.

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:38.850
Makima nodded and encouraged her subordinates
to return to work.

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:40.339
Want an anomaly of your own?

00:11:40.339 --> 00:11:44.130
Check out www.scpswag.com for high-quality
SCP merch!

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:47.529
Now go check out “Rick and Morty More Powerful
Than SCP Foundation?

00:11:47.529 --> 00:11:52.850
Mad Scientist Battle!” and “SCP-096 VS
Siren Head” for more crazy crossovers!

